keywords:
  - large language models
  - model-as-a-service
  - service-level monitoring
  - API brokerage
  - behavioral consistency
  - energy statistics
abstract: >-
  Organizations routing workloads through aggregated large language model (LLM) brokers rely on declared model
  identifiers while the serving backend remains hidden. We present HuePrint, a black-box framework that audits
  brokered endpoint consistency without weights or token probabilities. HuePrint elicits compact color codes and
  compares responses via regularized RGB energy and hybrid scoring, turning nearby outputs into continuous geometric
  distance. Across 38,688 cloud responses (56 endpoints, 12 backends), HuePrint lowers 30-call/side equal error rates
  (EERs) over word baselines from 6.25-8.04 to 3.49-5.00 percent on 20 locked endpoints (0.00 percent by 60-150
  calls/side). On those endpoints, it averages 5.18 percent within-family EER, outperforming LLMmap (10.53-34.39
  percent) and cost-matched continuation kernels (11.09-19.47 percent); unlike LLMmap, it avoids safety-triggering
  probes and runs over 15,000 times faster locally. Hybrid scoring cuts cross-provider EER to 5.93 percent, while
  two-stage confirmation drops false alerts from 14 to 1 across 100 same-label windows under one cent.
